      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Zayd would likely let the adventurers' aggression wash over him with a slow, deliberate smile, perhaps raising a hand in a gesture of gentle dismissal. He might begin, \"Patience, esteemed travelers; the sands teach us that haste is the quickest path to dust.\" He would then use flowery language, perhaps addressing them with a formal title like \"Honored Seekers of Fortune,\" before delicately suggesting their current fervor is unbecoming of those who wish to conduct serious trade. This approach subtly implies they are uncivilized brutes interrupting a sacred exchange.",
